Bug: push by name finds nothing when only -getproject has run

-olcxpushname is not in the "N of M compilation units need reparsing" check in
src/server.c, so with the project merely locked by -getproject nothing is
parsed. The first push answers "No symbol found" and the following -browse-next
calls then report an empty stack. The -p option used to mask this by getting
the project scanned before any request.

Same defect as test_browsing_push_name_parses_whole_project, and the fix is the
same: add OP_BROWSE_PUSH_NAME to that check. Warming the file with another
request first was tried and abandoned, because push by name then resolves 'i'
to whichever symbol was looked at last instead of the struct field at 10:22
that expected records. Remove this file when the check is fixed.
